The legal text is the Constitution of the Arab Republic of Egypt (2014, with the amendments approved by referendum
in April 2019), in the English translation published by the State Information Service
(https://sis.gov.eg/media/67726/dustor-eng.pdf), retrieved 29 October 2026. The PDF states no licence; the
official Arabic text is the authoritative one. The translation's own typing errors are kept as printed.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; headings, page numbers and footnote markers were left out; and the
versions were arranged as git commits credited to the publisher. The wording of the law was not changed. The
publisher does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
